Project Overview

The backend structure is designed for an educational video management system similar to Udemy, integrated within an e-commerce portal but extracted as a standalone product. The system uses a monolithic, modular architecture to allow future scalability and possible service extraction when needed.

Technologies

Framework: Next.js API Routes (Backend via Next.js functions)

Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL with Row-Level Security)

Authentication: Supabase Auth

API Style: REST

Core Concepts

Modular Monolith: Each domain (video, course, user, role, document) is structured in isolated modules within the monolith to allow future microservice extraction.

CQRS pattern will be optionally applied inside modules where needed.

Modules

User Management

User registration via Supabase Auth

Role assignment by Admin (User, Team Lead, Admin, Guest)

Guest users can view limited content

Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

Admin: Full access, including user and role management

Team Lead: Can create/manage courses, assign videos to users

User: Can view assigned videos and courses

Guest: Can view limited content only

Video Management

Video metadata includes: title, description, YouTube URL/ID, duration, category, tags

Automatic data fetch from YouTube API on video add

Filter and search by category/tags/keywords

Video preview available

Course Management

Courses contain ordered list of videos

Metadata: title, description, isMandatory

Course progress tracking based on video completion

Assignment Management

Assign video(s) or course(s) to users

Bulk assignments supported

Tracking of assigned items and completion status

Video Watch Log

Start time, watched duration, complete flag per user/video

Watch history used to calculate course progress

Comments

Users can leave comments per video

Admin moderation supported

Notification System

New assignment notifications

Reminders for incomplete or overdue content

Document System (Markdown-Based)

Notion-style markdown editor for text-based course materials

Documents can be:

Linked to courses

Available as general learning resources

Future Scalability

Easily extractable modules for microservice transition

All modules follow clear boundaries and interface contracts

Events can be emitted internally if needed for future message-based systems (Kafka, PubSub, etc.)

Deployment

Vercel (Next.js hosting)

Supabase (hosted backend + DB)

Summary

This backend structure provides a clean, scalable foundation with Supabase and Next.js. By using a modular monolithic pattern, we ensure fast MVP development while leaving room for future transformation into a more distributed architecture. 